-- title:
--   Regularity at a supersingular node gives localised membership
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`, stated as $\mathrm{red}\,c = 0 \iff c \in \mathfrak m_A$). Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2} = a$ and $a \in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$. Let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1 \cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series. Assume: the Laurent series of $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A red`, the localisation of the modular ring over $A$ at the prime ideal of elements with vanishing reduction (so $f \cdot s = r$ for some $r,s$ in that ring with $s$ of nonzero reduction), its image under `modularRedLocHom` lies in the subfield `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` of $k$-Laurent series generated by the two level-one $q$-expansion generators, and this image is nonzero; and the same three conditions for `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q) f`. Assume further (`hford`) that for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — a proper valuation subring containing the base field and a principal ideal ring — which is centred at the node $(a, a^q)$, in the sense that there are $x, y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$, $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^q$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j - x) > 0$, $W.\mathrm{ord}(j(q\,\cdot) - y) > 0$ for the two modular generators $j$ and its $q$-expansion twist, one has $W.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$. Then the Laurent series of $f$ lies in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A red a (a ^ q)`: there are polynomials $r, s$ in two variables over $A$ with `pointEval` of $s$ at $(a, a^q)$ nonzero in $k$ and $f \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$.
--
--   This is the supersingular case of the assertion that a modular function on $X_0(q)$ which has neither zero nor pole at any place centred at a supersingular node of the Deligne–Rapoport model in characteristic $q$ is a regular function there, i.e. lies in the local ring of the node, presented as a localisation of the two-variable node ring over the valuation ring $A$. It is used in the construction of elements with prescribed value at a Frobenius node pair, via `exists_mem_and_red_eq_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_centred_of_ssJSet`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_mem_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_mem_modularLocalized_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_ssJSet.lean

